{"run_id":"run_d8bd929af70f","schema_version":"0.1","seq":11,"t_ms":11,"text":"Here's how access requests are provisioned and reviewed, based on the internal \"IT access request process\" document:\n\n1. **Access by role:** Your job role determines your standard access.\n2. **Requests outside your role:** Anything beyond your role's standard access needs a named approver.\n3. **Quarterly review:** Access granted outside a role is reviewed every quarter.\n4. **Service accounts:** These are reviewed on the same quarterly cycle and must name a human owner.\n\nThe document is short. It doesn't say how to submit a request, who can be an approver, how long provisioning takes, or what happens to access that fails a review. For those, ask IT directly, or I can file a ticket in the IT support queue.","turn":3,"type":"agent.message"}
